sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant U as Streamlit UI
  participant A as FastAPI
  participant O as Orchestrator
  participant S as Supervisor
  participant C as ControlTools
  participant X as TaskExecutor
  participant W as GenericWorker
  participant B as SecondBrainRuntime
  participant M as MCP server

  U->>A: POST /requests
  A->>A: reserve request id and write RequestRecord
  A-->>U: submitted record
  A->>O: submit Request in background task
  O->>O: reserve id, await request semaphore
  O->>S: construct Supervisor
  S->>B: get_registry
  B-->>S: REGISTRY.md
  S->>W: create_agent with supervisor role and control tools only

  loop until Supervisor is done
    S->>W: run_step
    W->>W: LLM turn, then dispatch authorization per tool call
    alt delegation or escalation resolution
      W->>C: delegate_task or resolve_escalation
      C->>B: validate domain exists
      C-->>S: Task plus TaskState in pending batch
    end
    S->>S: detach pending batch
    loop concurrent batch, semaphore capped
      S->>X: execute task and task_state
      X->>B: load DOMAIN.md for each authorized domain
      X->>X: derive allowed tools from TrustedDomainGrants
      X->>M: get_tools existence check
      X->>W: fresh Task Worker with get_skill and execution tools
      W->>B: get_skill when needed
      B-->>W: SkillProjection
      W->>M: execution tool calls
      W->>W: structured finalization
      W-->>X: WorkerTaskResult or WorkerIterationExhausted
      X-->>S: TaskOutcome
    end
    S->>S: apply_outcome, validate escalation, persist BLOCKED state
    S->>W: append bounded outcome JSON to context
    opt BLOCKED escalation approved or denied
      W->>C: resolve_escalation on a later step
      C->>S: apply_decision, same task_id, attempt plus one
      S->>X: retry Task in the next batch
    end
  end

  S-->>O: final result
  O-->>A: result
  A->>A: mark record completed or failed
